From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 08:52:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] crypt32: Read a GeneralizedTime's fraction of a second as
 milliseconds.

Up to three digits were read as a number of milliseconds, so ".5" was
five of them, and with fewer than three before the Z the Z was read as a
digit and the time failed.  Windows 11 reads ".5" as 500 ms and drops
digits after the third, as RFC 3161 time stamps need.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/dlls/crypt32/decode.c b/dlls/crypt32/decode.c
index 72036a2c724..686525a9048 100644
--- a/dlls/crypt32/decode.c
+++ b/dlls/crypt32/decode.c
@@ -5052,14 +5052,18 @@ static BOOL CRYPT_AsnDecodeGeneralizedTime(const BYTE *pbEncoded,
                     if (ret && len > 0 && (*pbEncoded == '.' ||
                      *pbEncoded == ','))
                     {
-                        BYTE digits;
+                        WORD scale = 100;
 
+                        /* the fraction of a second, to the millisecond:
+                         * further digits are dropped
+                         */
                         pbEncoded++;
                         len--;
-                        /* workaround macro weirdness */
-                        digits = min(len, 3);
-                        CRYPT_TIME_GET_DIGITS(pbEncoded, len, digits,
-                         sysTime.wMilliseconds);
+                        for (; len > 0 && isdigit(*pbEncoded); pbEncoded++, len--)
+                        {
+                            sysTime.wMilliseconds += (*pbEncoded - '0') * scale;
+                            scale /= 10;
+                        }
                     }
                     if (ret)
                         ret = CRYPT_AsnDecodeTimeZone(pbEncoded, len,
